## Goal-Mode Multi-Task Contract

- Use the host product's Goal mode as the only long-running manager for initiatives with multiple issues or OpenSpec changes.
- The main Goal thread is manager-only: resolve dependencies, delegate one bounded unit, verify evidence, integrate accepted output, then select the next unit. Do not implement product code in the manager checkout.
- One write-capable worker owns exactly one issue, one OpenSpec `changeId`, and one repository-local orchestrator worktree.
- The worker runs the repository `orchestrator`; during implementation it uses `openspec-apply-change <changeId>` and follows `openspec instructions apply --change <changeId>`.
- Delegate only through the active host's native subagent tools. Never launch a recursive `codex exec`, `claude`, `cursor-agent`, or equivalent shell CLI, never poll its PTY, and never add a project-owned manager daemon as a fallback.
- Launch workers with no inherited turns or the smallest bounded positive history supported by the host; pass exact manifest/OpenSpec/orchestrator paths as the evidence package. Full-history forks are not the default.
- Wait on native completion/message events with one long wait. Do not heartbeat with repeated status/list calls. At a human gate, report once and stop that dependency edge.
- Treat configured worker/review model names as native-tool preferences. If a model is unavailable, use a compatible native or inherited model and record the fallback.
- Do not launch dependent work until the prior change has clean/accepted review evidence, {% if orchestrator_full_verify_policy == "on-request" %}affected verification{% else %}full verification{% endif %}, terminal OpenSpec sync/archive, and its accepted commit is integrated into the next worker's base.
- Rehydrate initiative state from `.ai/context/initiatives/<slug>/issues-manifest.json`, the selected OpenSpec change, and orchestrator run JSON. Do not create a second Goal ledger.
- Pause at repository, conflict, approval, live MR, deployment, failed full-suite, and explicit human-decision boundaries.
- Before review, record passing scoped test/lint and a handoff note for the current fingerprint. Run full verify {% if orchestrator_full_verify_policy == "on-request" %}only on explicit user request{% else %}after a clean/low review{% endif %}. Automatic review is capped at initial review plus one delta-only closure review.
